      "writtenOn": "2021-12-20T21:37:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The goal is to zero out the stencil right? So depthFail is the case where the stencil passed and the depth failed. So (at least in the kNotEqual case) this should be kZero right? In general for cover step depthFail \u003d\u003d dsPass for normal or inverse right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "7a50d26da2b9fb96020412c6877c535618020305",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9beb34b6_d8c43aa4",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/render/StencilAndFillPathRenderer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T14:54:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so, but it\u0027s kind of subtle so I should add a comment, if you buy my argument here:\n- kZero would be correct, but maybe hurts perf relative to kKeep\n- because every pixel that fails the depth *should* have a zero stencil value already\n- but this is because the earlier stencil passes (which aren\u0027t shown yet) also test against the same depth buffer but do not write the depth\n- the high-level ordering ensures no intervening draws overlap the stencil buffer and the cover steps, so there won\u0027t be a case where the depth test passes for the stenciling step and then fails on the cover step\n- since the stencil steps use kKeep on the depth failure as well, so everything remains zero.\n\nThat\u0027s a fairly complex state to mentally manage, though, and if the only benefit is that we use kKeep instead of kZero here, I could be easily convinced that we should just have depthFail\u003d\u003ddsPass (which is already the case for the current kInverted DSS::Face instance). For the stenciling steps, I think the rule is that depthfail \u003d stencilFail",
      "parentUuid": "1df61af8_5384d7fc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "7a50d26da2b9fb96020412c6877c535618020305",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fd87748_b4158ab9",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/render/StencilAndFillPathRenderer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T15:09:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The depthFail is specifically for the case where stencil passes but the depth fails. So when this gets updtate to use stencil compare of kGreater that means the stencil specifically won\u0027t have a value of 0. Now it may be the case we never hits this use case in practice but I think we should treat it like the stencil is not zero since it passed the stencil test. Thus it needs to be reset to 0.",
      "parentUuid": "9beb34b6_d8c43aa4",
